[list]
[*]Fixed: a colonist who woke with a meal already in their pack ate breakfast in their sleepwear and changed back only afterwards. Eating is normally left alone when the food is already on the colonist, because on a work shift they are standing at their bench and a trip to the wardrobe buys nothing. A bedroom stand is the opposite case. They wake up beside it, so changing costs no walking at all, and skipping it sent them across the base in nightclothes and back again to change. Waking now changes them back before they go and eat, whether the meal is in a stockpile or in their own pack. Work and recreation stands behave exactly as before.
[/list]
